-- "2 to 6 months" range the rewrite drops), em dashes removed.
--
-- content_updated_at is set on purpose: this is a real content change, so the
-- guide shows "Updated" like an admin edit would (the hook does not run for raw SQL).
-- Idempotent: only applies while the old answer snippet is still in place.

UPDATE guides SET
  lede = $botox$Curious about how long the effects of Botox really last? For many cosmetic treatments, the effects last about three to four months, although the exact duration can vary between people and treatment areas. Find out what to expect as Botox starts working, how the results gradually wear off, what can affect how long it lasts, and how duration can vary by treatment area and botulinum toxin product. You’ll also find practical aftercare information and important safety considerations.$botox$,
  excerpt = $botox$Botox usually lasts about three to four months for cosmetic treatments. See the timeline, what affects duration, results by area and brand, and aftercare.$botox$,
  meta_description = $botox$Botox usually lasts about three to four months for cosmetic treatments. See the timeline, what affects duration, results by area and brand, and aftercare.$botox$,
  answer_snippet = $botox$Botox commonly provides cosmetic results for around three to four months, but the exact duration varies. Factors such as the treatment area, amount used, individual response, and treatment technique can influence how long the effects remain noticeable. Areas with frequent muscle movement may show returning movement sooner.$botox$,
  at_a_glance = $botox$["Botox commonly lasts around three to four months for cosmetic treatments, although individual results can vary.", "Visible effects usually begin developing within several days and continue to build, with the full effect generally assessed at around two weeks.", "Duration can be influenced by the treatment area, amount used, muscle activity, individual response, and injection technique. These factors should not be treated as fixed predictors for every patient.", "Repeated treatment may change how much treatment is needed or how frequently it is required, but the amount and timing should be decided individually rather than assumed to decrease predictably.", "Stopping Botox does not make you age faster. As the effect wears off, treated muscles gradually return toward their usual movement, and wrinkles may become visible again."]$botox$::jsonb,
  faq = $botox$[{"question": "What happens after 10 years of Botox?", "answer": "After 10 years of repeated Botox treatment, long-term effects remain uncertain because research is limited. Studies suggest repeated injections may cause changes in treated muscles, including reduced muscle activity and muscle thinning. However, the review does not establish that long-term cosmetic Botox is harmful or that these changes occur in everyone.", "detail": "If you have been receiving Botox for many years, discuss your treatment history, benefits, risks, and ongoing treatment plan with your clinician."}, {"question": "Do you age faster after stopping Botox?", "answer": "No. When Botox wears off, the treated muscles gradually return toward their usual movement. Lines that were previously reduced may become visible again, but stopping Botox does not cause the ageing process to speed up."}, {"question": "Which lasts longer, Botox or filler?", "answer": "There is no single answer because fillers differ by product and treatment area. Some fillers can last considerably longer than Botox, but their lifespan varies. Botox reduces muscle activity, while fillers add volume, so the appropriate option depends on what is being treated."}, {"question": "Can Botox last six months?", "answer": "A six-month duration has been reported for some botulinum toxin treatments, but the duration can vary depending on the product, treatment area, and individual response. The source discusses a newer botulinum toxin treatment and its reported six-month results."}]$botox$::jsonb,
  sources = $botox$[{"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26863598/", "title": "Efficacy and Safety of OnabotulinumtoxinA Treatment of Forehead Lines: A Multicenter, Randomized, Dose-Ranging Controlled Trial", "publisher": "Dermatologic Surgery", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2016", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23106853/", "title": "OnabotulinumtoxinA: a meta-analysis of duration of effect in the treatment of glabellar lines", "publisher": "Dermatologic Surgery", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2012", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27110893/", "title": "Duration of Clinical Efficacy of OnabotulinumtoxinA in Crow's Feet Lines: Results from Two Multicenter, Randomized, Controlled Trials", "publisher": "Dermatologic Surgery", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2016", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35176198/", "title": "Efficacy of botulinum toxin in masseter muscle hypertrophy for lower face contouring", "publisher": "Journal of Cosmetic Dermatology", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2022", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://www.rxabbvie.com/pdf/botox_pi.pdf", "title": "BOTOX (onabotulinumtoxinA) Prescribing Information", "publisher": "AbbVie", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40377719/", "title": "The lip flip: a systematic review of botulinum toxin lip augmentation", "publisher": "Archives of Dermatological Research", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2025", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21197522/", "title": "Rapid onset of response and patient-reported outcomes after onabotulinumtoxinA treatment of moderate-to-severe glabellar lines", "publisher": "Journal of Drugs in Dermatology", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2011", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33488922/", "title": "Onset and Duration of AbobotulinumtoxinA for Aesthetic Use in the Upper Face: A Systematic Literature Review", "publisher": "The Journal of Clinical and Aesthetic Dermatology", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2020", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21745254/", "title": "Time to onset of response of abobotulinumtoxinA in the treatment of glabellar lines: a subset analysis of phase 3 clinical trials of a new botulinum toxin type A", "publisher": "Dermatologic Surgery", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2011", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24098087/", "title": "Onset and duration of effect of incobotulinumtoxinA, onabotulinumtoxinA, and abobotulinumtoxinA in the treatment of glabellar frown lines: a randomized, double-blind study", "publisher": "Clinical, Cosmetic and Investigational Dermatology", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2013", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30893162/", "title": "Efficacy and Safety of PrabotulinumtoxinA for the Treatment of Glabellar Lines in Adult Subjects: Results From 2 Identical Phase III Studies", "publisher": "Dermatologic Surgery", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2019", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38828475/", "title": "Real-World Patient Experience With PrabotulinumtoxinA in the United Kingdom: A Single-Center Survey and Analysis of 254 Patients", "publisher": "Aesthetic Surgery Journal Open Forum", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2024", "claimsSupported": []}, {"url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31791824/", "title": "DaxibotulinumtoxinA for Injection has a prolonged duration of response in the treatment of glabellar lines: Pooled data from two multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 3 studies (SAKURA 1 and SAKURA 2)", "publisher": "Journal of the American Academy of Dermatology", "sourceType": "primary", "publishedDate": "2020", "claimsSupported": []}]$botox$::jsonb,
  sources_count = 13,
  body = $botox${"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox is a temporary treatment, so understanding how long its effects may last can help with realistic planning.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "For many cosmetic treatments, muscle movement gradually returns over several months as the effect wears off. The exact timeline varies, so there is no single duration that applies to everyone.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "FDA status", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA) has FDA-approved cosmetic and medical indications. Approved cosmetic indications include specific facial areas such as frown lines, crow’s feet, and forehead lines, while the labelling has also been updated to include platysma bands. Other uses, such as jaw slimming and a lip flip, are considered off-label uses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Because Botox has different approved indications, duration should always be discussed in relation to the specific treatment and area rather than treating all uses as equivalent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Why Botox is temporary: how it works", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox is a brand name for onabotulinumtoxinA, a botulinum toxin type A medicine. It temporarily reduces activity in treated muscles by interfering with nerve signals that trigger muscle contraction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When administered into a targeted facial muscle, the reduction in muscle activity can make wrinkles caused by repeated muscle contraction, such as frown lines, crow’s feet, and forehead lines, less noticeable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Unlike dermal fillers, which add volume beneath the skin, Botox works by reducing muscle activity rather than replacing lost volume.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The effects are temporary because nerve-to-muscle communication gradually recovers. As movement returns, treated lines may become visible again.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Stopping Botox does not make you age faster or automatically make your wrinkles worse. Your treated muscles gradually return toward their usual movement as the effects wear off.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The Botox timeline: onset, peak, and gradual wear-off", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox will not have immediate effects, so no dramatic changes are expected right after receiving injections.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "In the first few days, the process is still unfolding. Most patients start noticing the effects somewhere around day three or four, but it will continue to unfold over the next few days.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It is good to wait two weeks to evaluate the effect instead of making assumptions about how far the treatment has taken effect sooner.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "After reaching its peak effect, the results will start fading away over the following months. It should be noted that Botox fades out progressively and does not disappear at once. Due to returning muscle movement, lines may gradually start to appear again.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Depending on the type of procedure, for most cosmetic procedures of the upper face, signs of movement may start showing themselves several months after the procedure. However, this time may vary for each patient and procedure.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If you have an important event coming up, discuss treatment timing with your injector rather than relying on a fixed timeline. This allows time for the results to develop and for temporary treatment-related effects to settle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Your first treatment may also behave differently from later treatments. The amount used should be adjusted according to your individual anatomy, treatment goal, and response rather than assuming that everyone needs progressively more or less product.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "What affects how long your results last?", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is no single duration that applies to everyone. Several factors can influence how long the effects remain noticeable, and some commonly repeated explanations are not strong enough to predict exactly when Botox will wear off.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Metabolism", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Individual biological differences may affect how people respond to treatment, but metabolism should not be presented as a definite reason why Botox wears off faster in athletes or highly active people.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Muscle strength and size", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Muscle anatomy and activity can matter, but muscle size alone does not reliably explain how long Botox lasts. Treatment amount, anatomy, treatment purpose, and the outcome being measured can all affect the result.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Dose", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The amount of product used is an important treatment consideration, but a higher dose should not automatically be described as producing longer-lasting results. The appropriate amount depends on the treatment area, individual anatomy, and treatment goal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Treatment area", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Areas with frequent muscle movement may show returning movement sooner, but duration should be assessed according to the specific treatment area and clinical evidence rather than movement alone.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Injector technique", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Injection placement, treatment planning, and appropriate dosing can influence the treatment result. Choosing a qualified and appropriately trained injector is therefore important.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lifestyle", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Factors such as physical activity, sun exposure, smoking, and stress are sometimes suggested as influences on Botox longevity, but the evidence is not strong enough to present these factors as reliable predictors of how long an individual treatment will last.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Previous treatments", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "With repeated treatment, the amount needed and the interval between treatments may change for some people. But the frequency and dose of treatment should be evaluated on an individual basis since repeat injections do not necessarily mean smaller doses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "How long does Botox last in the treatment area?", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The treated area can influence how long Botox lasts. But treatment areas with different indications should not necessarily be combined because they can involve different medications, dosages, treatment purposes, and outcome measurements.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "For instance, the treatment of wrinkles on the face for cosmetic reasons is different from the treatment of excessive sweating on medical grounds. In the same way, jaw slimming and TMJ symptom treatment are two different outcomes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "(table) Treatment area | Approximate duration || Forehead lines | About 3–4 months ([PubMed study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26863598/)) || Frown lines | About 3–4 months ([PubMed meta-analysis](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23106853)) || Crow’s feet | About 3–4 months ([PubMed clinical trials](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27110893/)) || Masseter | Varies; studies report effects lasting 6–12 months. ([PubMed systematic review](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35176198)) || Underarms/hyperhidrosis | Median 201 days (~6.6 months) ([BOTOX prescribing information](https://www.rxabbvie.com/pdf/botox_pi.pdf)) || Lip flip | Varies; no established standard duration. ([PubMed systematic review](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40377719/))", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Duration by brand: Botox, Dysport, Xeomin, Jeuveau, and Daxxify", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "(table) Brand | Duration | Onset || Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA) | About 4 months ([PubMed: OnabotulinumtoxinA duration meta-analysis](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23106853/)) | About 2–4 days ([PubMed: Onabotulinumtoxin A onset study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21197522/)) || Dysport (abobotulinumtoxinA) | About 3–6 months across studies; 4 months most commonly reported ([PubMed: Systematic review of onset and duration](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33488922/)) | About 2–3 days ([PubMed: Phase 3 onset study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21745254/)) || Xeomin (incobotulinumtoxinA) | About 3–4 months ([PubMed: Randomised comparison of incobotulinumtoxinA, onabotulinumtoxinA and abobotulinumtoxinA](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24098087/)) | About 3 days ([PubMed: Randomised comparative study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24098087/)) || Jeuveau (prabotulinumtoxinA-xvfs) | Up to about 5 months in the Phase 3 study ([PubMed: PrabotulinumtoxinA Phase 3 study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30893162/)) | About 2–3 days ([PubMed: Jeuveau real-world onset study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38828475/)) || Daxxify (daxibotulinumtoxinA-lanm) | 24 weeks median for maintaining none-or-mild glabellar lines ([PubMed: SAKURA Phase 3 studies](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31791824/)) | Varies by product and endpoint", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Important note:", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Onset and duration depend on factors such as the drug, area treated, dose, design of the study, and endpoint used. These data are not interchangeable across different drugs and cannot be used as a guide for conversion to other dosages.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Additionally, it would not be correct to call Dysport \"3–4 months\", because the duration was found to vary from 3 to 6 months, with 4 months being the most common result in the systematic review.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Finally, 24 weeks for Daxxify is specific only to one endpoint in the glabellar lines treatment and not because all Daxxify procedures take 6 months.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "How to make your Botox results last longer", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is no proven way to extend the effect of one Botox injection by adding a certain amount of time (weeks/months).", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Stay consistent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Instead of scheduling your Botox injections at a fixed interval, consider following a schedule that has been created by you and your injector. While regular injections might help you maintain your desired look, they cannot serve as evidence that every single injection will work for a longer period of time.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Choose an experienced injector.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Appropriate assessment, product selection, dosing, and injection technique are important for achieving the intended result. They should not, however, be presented as a guarantee of longer duration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Aftercare", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Follow the advice of your injector about aftercare because the information you receive might depend on the procedure you have undergone. However, aftercare should not be considered a tool which can help Botox work for extra months.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Take care of your skin.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Daily sun protection, refraining from smoking, and overall care of your skin might improve the health condition of your skin. Nevertheless, it should not be considered a proven method of extending the clinical effects of Botox.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Be wary of \"longevity hacks\" that claim to prolong the effects of Botox treatment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is no solid proof of the effectiveness of supplements, special creams, or any other hacks that could prolong the effects of the Botox injection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Aftercare: protecting your results in the first 24 hours", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "After treatment, follow the specific aftercare instructions your injector provides.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Within the first few hours after your treatment:", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "listType": "bullet", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Avoid rubbing, massaging, or applying unnecessary pressure to the treated area unless your injector tells you otherwise.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Follow your injector’s advice about exercise and strenuous activity rather than treating a blanket 24-hour restriction as universal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal movement should not automatically be confused with a requirement to remain standing or upright for several hours.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Ask your injector about heat exposure, saunas, spas, and hot tubs because aftercare recommendations can vary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 5, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Alcohol should not be described as something that definitely causes bruising. If your clinician advises limiting it around treatment, follow that individualised advice.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 6, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Tell your injector about all prescription medicines, over-the-counter medicines, and supplements you take. Do not stop prescribed medication on your own.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Your injector’s instructions should take priority because aftercare recommendations may depend on the treatment and your individual circumstances.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Signs your Botox is wearing off and building a maintenance schedule", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox generally fades gradually rather than suddenly. One of the first changes you may notice is the return of movement in the treated area.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "For example, your eyebrows may become more mobile or lines may gradually become visible again.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "This does not mean the treatment has damaged your skin or caused premature ageing. It generally reflects the gradual return of muscle activity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When movement starts returning, contact your injector to discuss your results and an appropriate treatment schedule. The return of movement does not automatically mean that another injection is immediately appropriate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If your results consistently seem to wear off much sooner than expected, discuss the treatment amount, technique, treatment area, and timing with your injector rather than assuming that you simply need more Botox.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Safety, side effects, and honest limits", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox is a prescription medical treatment with potential benefits and risks. Before treatment, discuss your medical history, treatment goals, possible side effects, and whether the treatment is appropriate for you with a qualified clinician.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Common treatment-related effects can include bruising, redness, swelling, and headache. Temporary effects such as eyelid or eyebrow drooping, asymmetry, or an unwanted change in facial movement can also occur. Persistent or concerning symptoms should be assessed rather than assuming they will always resolve without medical attention.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Seek immediate medical attention if you develop difficulty breathing, swallowing, or speaking after treatment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It is also important to remember that Botox does not last forever. Maintaining the result generally involves additional treatments, which means additional cost. Pricing can vary depending on the provider, location, product, treatment area, and amount used.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox and dermal fillers are not the same. Fillers add volume, while Botox reduces muscle activity. Their duration and uses are also different, so one should not be treated as a direct substitute for the other.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Last but not least, choose a qualified and appropriately licensed professional. A qualified injector can assess your anatomy, treatment goals, and medical history and help determine an appropriate treatment plan.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}]}}$botox$::jsonb,
  content_updated_at = now(),
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'how-long-does-botox-last'
  AND answer_snippet LIKE 'Botox typically lasts about three to four months for most cosmetic treatments, with a normal range%';

-- Production got this rewrite on 2026-10-28 by direct SQL, before the table
-- link renderer was deployed there, so its two tables carry plain "(PubMed
-- study)" text instead of links. Swap in the linked body above, but only while
-- that exact plain body (md5 below) is still in place, so an admin edit is never
-- overwritten. No-op everywhere else, staging included. Same content, so the
-- Updated date is left alone.
UPDATE guides SET
  body = $botox${"root": {"type": "root", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox is a temporary treatment, so understanding how long its effects may last can help with realistic planning.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "For many cosmetic treatments, muscle movement gradually returns over several months as the effect wears off. The exact timeline varies, so there is no single duration that applies to everyone.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "FDA status", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA) has FDA-approved cosmetic and medical indications. Approved cosmetic indications include specific facial areas such as frown lines, crow’s feet, and forehead lines, while the labelling has also been updated to include platysma bands. Other uses, such as jaw slimming and a lip flip, are considered off-label uses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Because Botox has different approved indications, duration should always be discussed in relation to the specific treatment and area rather than treating all uses as equivalent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Why Botox is temporary: how it works", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox is a brand name for onabotulinumtoxinA, a botulinum toxin type A medicine. It temporarily reduces activity in treated muscles by interfering with nerve signals that trigger muscle contraction.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When administered into a targeted facial muscle, the reduction in muscle activity can make wrinkles caused by repeated muscle contraction, such as frown lines, crow’s feet, and forehead lines, less noticeable.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Unlike dermal fillers, which add volume beneath the skin, Botox works by reducing muscle activity rather than replacing lost volume.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The effects are temporary because nerve-to-muscle communication gradually recovers. As movement returns, treated lines may become visible again.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Stopping Botox does not make you age faster or automatically make your wrinkles worse. Your treated muscles gradually return toward their usual movement as the effects wear off.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The Botox timeline: onset, peak, and gradual wear-off", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox will not have immediate effects, so no dramatic changes are expected right after receiving injections.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "In the first few days, the process is still unfolding. Most patients start noticing the effects somewhere around day three or four, but it will continue to unfold over the next few days.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It is good to wait two weeks to evaluate the effect instead of making assumptions about how far the treatment has taken effect sooner.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "After reaching its peak effect, the results will start fading away over the following months. It should be noted that Botox fades out progressively and does not disappear at once. Due to returning muscle movement, lines may gradually start to appear again.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Depending on the type of procedure, for most cosmetic procedures of the upper face, signs of movement may start showing themselves several months after the procedure. However, this time may vary for each patient and procedure.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If you have an important event coming up, discuss treatment timing with your injector rather than relying on a fixed timeline. This allows time for the results to develop and for temporary treatment-related effects to settle.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Your first treatment may also behave differently from later treatments. The amount used should be adjusted according to your individual anatomy, treatment goal, and response rather than assuming that everyone needs progressively more or less product.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "What affects how long your results last?", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is no single duration that applies to everyone. Several factors can influence how long the effects remain noticeable, and some commonly repeated explanations are not strong enough to predict exactly when Botox will wear off.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Metabolism", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Individual biological differences may affect how people respond to treatment, but metabolism should not be presented as a definite reason why Botox wears off faster in athletes or highly active people.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Muscle strength and size", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Muscle anatomy and activity can matter, but muscle size alone does not reliably explain how long Botox lasts. Treatment amount, anatomy, treatment purpose, and the outcome being measured can all affect the result.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Dose", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The amount of product used is an important treatment consideration, but a higher dose should not automatically be described as producing longer-lasting results. The appropriate amount depends on the treatment area, individual anatomy, and treatment goal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Treatment area", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Areas with frequent muscle movement may show returning movement sooner, but duration should be assessed according to the specific treatment area and clinical evidence rather than movement alone.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Injector technique", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Injection placement, treatment planning, and appropriate dosing can influence the treatment result. Choosing a qualified and appropriately trained injector is therefore important.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Lifestyle", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Factors such as physical activity, sun exposure, smoking, and stress are sometimes suggested as influences on Botox longevity, but the evidence is not strong enough to present these factors as reliable predictors of how long an individual treatment will last.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h3", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Previous treatments", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "With repeated treatment, the amount needed and the interval between treatments may change for some people. But the frequency and dose of treatment should be evaluated on an individual basis since repeat injections do not necessarily mean smaller doses.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "How long does Botox last in the treatment area?", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "The treated area can influence how long Botox lasts. But treatment areas with different indications should not necessarily be combined because they can involve different medications, dosages, treatment purposes, and outcome measurements.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "For instance, the treatment of wrinkles on the face for cosmetic reasons is different from the treatment of excessive sweating on medical grounds. In the same way, jaw slimming and TMJ symptom treatment are two different outcomes.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "(table) Treatment area | Approximate duration || Forehead lines | About 3–4 months ([PubMed study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26863598/)) || Frown lines | About 3–4 months ([PubMed meta-analysis](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23106853)) || Crow’s feet | About 3–4 months ([PubMed clinical trials](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27110893/)) || Masseter | Varies; studies report effects lasting 6–12 months. ([PubMed systematic review](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35176198)) || Underarms/hyperhidrosis | Median 201 days (~6.6 months) ([BOTOX prescribing information](https://www.rxabbvie.com/pdf/botox_pi.pdf)) || Lip flip | Varies; no established standard duration. ([PubMed systematic review](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40377719/))", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Duration by brand: Botox, Dysport, Xeomin, Jeuveau, and Daxxify", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "(table) Brand | Duration | Onset || Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA) | About 4 months ([PubMed: OnabotulinumtoxinA duration meta-analysis](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23106853/)) | About 2–4 days ([PubMed: Onabotulinumtoxin A onset study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21197522/)) || Dysport (abobotulinumtoxinA) | About 3–6 months across studies; 4 months most commonly reported ([PubMed: Systematic review of onset and duration](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33488922/)) | About 2–3 days ([PubMed: Phase 3 onset study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21745254/)) || Xeomin (incobotulinumtoxinA) | About 3–4 months ([PubMed: Randomised comparison of incobotulinumtoxinA, onabotulinumtoxinA and abobotulinumtoxinA](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24098087/)) | About 3 days ([PubMed: Randomised comparative study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24098087/)) || Jeuveau (prabotulinumtoxinA-xvfs) | Up to about 5 months in the Phase 3 study ([PubMed: PrabotulinumtoxinA Phase 3 study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30893162/)) | About 2–3 days ([PubMed: Jeuveau real-world onset study](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38828475/)) || Daxxify (daxibotulinumtoxinA-lanm) | 24 weeks median for maintaining none-or-mild glabellar lines ([PubMed: SAKURA Phase 3 studies](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31791824/)) | Varies by product and endpoint", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Important note:", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Onset and duration depend on factors such as the drug, area treated, dose, design of the study, and endpoint used. These data are not interchangeable across different drugs and cannot be used as a guide for conversion to other dosages.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Additionally, it would not be correct to call Dysport \"3–4 months\", because the duration was found to vary from 3 to 6 months, with 4 months being the most common result in the systematic review.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Finally, 24 weeks for Daxxify is specific only to one endpoint in the glabellar lines treatment and not because all Daxxify procedures take 6 months.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "How to make your Botox results last longer", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is no proven way to extend the effect of one Botox injection by adding a certain amount of time (weeks/months).", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Stay consistent.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Instead of scheduling your Botox injections at a fixed interval, consider following a schedule that has been created by you and your injector. While regular injections might help you maintain your desired look, they cannot serve as evidence that every single injection will work for a longer period of time.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Choose an experienced injector.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Appropriate assessment, product selection, dosing, and injection technique are important for achieving the intended result. They should not, however, be presented as a guarantee of longer duration.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Aftercare", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Follow the advice of your injector about aftercare because the information you receive might depend on the procedure you have undergone. However, aftercare should not be considered a tool which can help Botox work for extra months.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Take care of your skin.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Daily sun protection, refraining from smoking, and overall care of your skin might improve the health condition of your skin. Nevertheless, it should not be considered a proven method of extending the clinical effects of Botox.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Be wary of \"longevity hacks\" that claim to prolong the effects of Botox treatment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 1, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "There is no solid proof of the effectiveness of supplements, special creams, or any other hacks that could prolong the effects of the Botox injection.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Aftercare: protecting your results in the first 24 hours", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "After treatment, follow the specific aftercare instructions your injector provides.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Within the first few hours after your treatment:", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "ul", "type": "list", "listType": "bullet", "start": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"type": "listitem", "value": 1, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Avoid rubbing, massaging, or applying unnecessary pressure to the treated area unless your injector tells you otherwise.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 2, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Follow your injector’s advice about exercise and strenuous activity rather than treating a blanket 24-hour restriction as universal.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 3, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Normal movement should not automatically be confused with a requirement to remain standing or upright for several hours.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 4, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Ask your injector about heat exposure, saunas, spas, and hot tubs because aftercare recommendations can vary.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 5, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Alcohol should not be described as something that definitely causes bruising. If your clinician advises limiting it around treatment, follow that individualised advice.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "listitem", "value": 6, "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Tell your injector about all prescription medicines, over-the-counter medicines, and supplements you take. Do not stop prescribed medication on your own.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Your injector’s instructions should take priority because aftercare recommendations may depend on the treatment and your individual circumstances.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Signs your Botox is wearing off and building a maintenance schedule", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox generally fades gradually rather than suddenly. One of the first changes you may notice is the return of movement in the treated area.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "For example, your eyebrows may become more mobile or lines may gradually become visible again.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "This does not mean the treatment has damaged your skin or caused premature ageing. It generally reflects the gradual return of muscle activity.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "When movement starts returning, contact your injector to discuss your results and an appropriate treatment schedule. The return of movement does not automatically mean that another injection is immediately appropriate.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "If your results consistently seem to wear off much sooner than expected, discuss the treatment amount, technique, treatment area, and timing with your injector rather than assuming that you simply need more Botox.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"tag": "h2", "type": "heading", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Safety, side effects, and honest limits", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox is a prescription medical treatment with potential benefits and risks. Before treatment, discuss your medical history, treatment goals, possible side effects, and whether the treatment is appropriate for you with a qualified clinician.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Common treatment-related effects can include bruising, redness, swelling, and headache. Temporary effects such as eyelid or eyebrow drooping, asymmetry, or an unwanted change in facial movement can also occur. Persistent or concerning symptoms should be assessed rather than assuming they will always resolve without medical attention.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Seek immediate medical attention if you develop difficulty breathing, swallowing, or speaking after treatment.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "It is also important to remember that Botox does not last forever. Maintaining the result generally involves additional treatments, which means additional cost. Pricing can vary depending on the provider, location, product, treatment area, and amount used.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Botox and dermal fillers are not the same. Fillers add volume, while Botox reduces muscle activity. Their duration and uses are also different, so one should not be treated as a direct substitute for the other.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "format": "", "indent": 0, "version": 1, "children": [{"mode": "normal", "text": "Last but not least, choose a qualified and appropriately licensed professional. A qualified injector can assess your anatomy, treatment goals, and medical history and help determine an appropriate treatment plan.", "type": "text", "style": "", "format": 0, "version": 1}]}]}}$botox$::jsonb,
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'how-long-does-botox-last'
  AND md5(body::text) = 'c4db032452f223f2682a7311c582a276';
